  "id": "Compound::DB00200 - Gene::8029",
  "verbalization": "Hydroxocobalamin appears to interact with Cubn through a shared pathway involving cobalamin binding. The evidence suggests that Hydroxocobalamin binds to Mmachc or Tcn1, which in turn participate in cobalamin binding, a process that Cubn is involved in. This indicates that Hydroxocobalamin may influence Cubn through a common intermediate step in the cobalamin binding pathway. The high scores in all three paths suggest a consistent relationship, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains unclear. The presence of multiple binding sites and the involvement of different proteins in the cobalamin binding process highlight the complexity of the interaction, but the core link between Hydroxocobalamin and Cubn appears to be through the cobalamin binding pathway.",
